# Linux CUDA runtime. Keep vLLM aligned with deploy/Dockerfile.accurate.
# Known exception: setuptools stays at 80.10.2 because vLLM 0.30.0 requires setuptools<81. The
# three advisories against it (fixed in 83.0.0 and 84.1.0) concern building source distributions
# and legacy wheel installs on Windows, which this Linux runtime image does not do.
-e ./MinerU[torch]
.[accurate,telemetry,telemetry-sdk]
vllm==0.30.0
# Security floors: the base image ships older releases with published advisories. certifi
# 2026.7.22 bundles root certificates with compromised intermediate keys (fixed in 2026.10.18);
# aiohttp 3.14.3 has eleven high-severity advisories (fixed in 3.14.4), filelock 4.0.1 and
# pyjwt 2.14.0 have advisories fixed in 4.2.1 and 2.15.0; dnspython 2.8.0 and opentelemetry-api
# 1.40.0 have denial-of-service advisories (fixed in 2.9.2 and 1.45.2). The compile lifts the rest of OpenTelemetry to the same release line. Known cost:
# pip check then also reports two base packages this service does not use (lmcache asks for
# opentelemetry-api<=1.40.0, the Prometheus exporter for sdk~=1.40); the base's own pip check
# already fails on other packages.
certifi>=2026.10.18
dnspython>=2.9.2
opentelemetry-api>=1.45.2
aiohttp>=3.14.4
filelock>=4.2.1
pyjwt>=2.15.0
